<title>USA: US aluminum service center shipments up in Jan-May.</title>
<headline>US aluminum service center shipments up in Jan-May.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-07-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. service center shipments of aluminum mill products for the five months ended May were up 9.1 percent above shipments for the same period in 1996, the National Association of Aluminum Distributors reported.</p>
<p>According to NAAD's three month moving average index, shipments in May rose to 101.5 points compared with 100 points in April, while inventory fell to 103.8 points in May from 104.4 in April, and 104.9 points in May 1996.</p>
<p>The number of months inventory is now down to 2.8, the lowest since 2.2 months of stock back in January 1996.</p>
<p>((New York Commodity Desk 212-859-1646))</p>
